{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794646669,"nonce":"F4bh/x7uFmIIKxyzKwYjFH+wMWg=","title":"A FLIP slide carried by a binding is never released in a window","message":"241a0233 gives a FLIP slide a motion binding of its own, taken away by `release_flip_bindings` inside `apply_flip_animation_props`. A window applies animation values only on a frame in which a tick found something running. `tick_flip_animations` returned false on the frame a slide finished, since it had already removed the animation, so that frame never applied and the binding was never released. It stayed marked as playing, so the scheduler kept asking for frames at rest (about 20 a second in flip_window_check after the first slide), and the card stayed where the last step put it.\n\nThe harness did not show it: `Headless` applied animation values on every frame. It now has `gate_animation_apply`, which applies them as the window does, and the path tests use it.\n\nFix: the tick answers true while a finished slide still has its binding on a node, until the apply has released it, so a skipped frame does not lose the signal (the first attempt answered true for the finishing frame only, and the window's skipped frames consumed it). The redraw check for visible FLIP work counts a pending release too. Test: `a_flip_slide_leaves_nothing_bound_when_it_ends`.\n\nWindow trace of flip_window_check at rest between slides, drawn frames asked for by: scheduler, external, scheduler_raw before; external, scheduler_raw after, which is what the baked configuration shows.","files":null}]}